// cardInfographic is a static, human-designed infographic for a card page.
//
// The page keeps the card art and adds a compact "Infographic / Expand" bar
// under it (sidebar on desktop, header card on mobile) that opens the full image
// in a viewer. It is not placed inline: at the article column's width the image
// renders at under half its designed size, which leaves its body text too small
// to read in place.
//
// Images are committed by slug and generated by scripts/infographic-images.sh:
// static/img/infographic-<slug>.jpg is the full 1024x1536 image and
// infographic-<slug>-teaser.jpg is the bar's thumbnail, its top 1024x640 region
// at 256x160.
type cardInfographic struct {
	// Alt names the image briefly. Its content is in Text, which the viewer offers
	// as a collapsed "Text version" below the image: a 1,500-character alt string
	// is read as one unbroken run with no structure to navigate.
	Alt string
	// Text is the image's content as plain sentences, one per section, rendered as
	// a list in the viewer's collapsed "Text version". It is the only way a
	// screen-reader user gets what the image says, so it transcribes every figure
	// and caveat the image states.
	Text []string
	// Checked is when the image's figures were last verified. It is shown in the
	// caption because, unlike page prose, an image cannot be corrected by a reseed.
	Checked string
	// Facts are figures the image states. TestCardInfographics_FactsMatchCardProse
	// fails when one no longer appears in the card's cards.json text or in Text.
	// It checks the seed file only: admin edits and approved card updates change
	// the live prose without touching cards.json, so recheck the image when one of
	// those lands on a card that has an infographic.
	Facts []string
}

